---
// Terms of service (WWW-6). Drafted by the dev team; the client reviews it.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT, LEGAL_VERSION, readSettings } from '../settings.ts';

const s = readSettings(process.env);
const updated = new Date(`${LEGAL_VERSION}T00:00:00Z`).toLocaleDateString('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
  timeZone: 'UTC',
});
---

<Base
  title="Terms of service"
  description="The terms for using OmniBridge: accounts, acceptable use, your channel accounts, data processing, eBay and Amazon terms, liability and English law."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated} (version {LEGAL_VERSION})</p>

    <h2>1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      OmniBridge is a back-office service for sellers on Amazon, eBay and their own websites,
      provided by {s.operatorLegalName} (“we”, “us”) to businesses (“customers”). These terms apply
      to every customer and to every person who uses OmniBridge for a customer (“users”).
    </p>

    <h2>2. Accounts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Each user has their own named account. Shared logins are not allowed.</li>
      <li>Every user must use two-step sign-in and keep their password and codes private.</li>
      <li>The customer’s admins decide who has access and what each user can see, and remove users who leave.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You must not:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>use OmniBridge for anything unlawful or to send unsolicited messages to buyers;</li>
      <li>try to reach another customer’s data, test or break our security without permission, or overload the service;</li>
      <li>copy, resell or reverse-engineer the service;</li>
      <li>use buyer data for anything other than fulfilling and supporting the buyer’s order.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Your channel accounts</h2>
    <p>
      You connect your own Amazon, eBay, website and carrier accounts and stay responsible for them:
      for following each platform’s rules, for the listings, prices and stock you publish, and for
      the orders you dispatch. You can disconnect an account at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Data processing</h2>
    <p>
      For personal data in your workspace you are the controller and we are your processor. Our data
      processing terms are part of these terms: we process personal data only on your instructions
      to provide the service; keep it confidential and secure; use only the sub-processors listed in
      our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> and tell you before adding one; help you answer data
      subject requests and report breaches without undue delay; delete buyers’ details within 30
      days of delivery; and delete or return your data when the service ends, keeping only what the
      law requires.
    </p>

    <h2>6. eBay terms for “Your Users”</h2>
    <p>
      If you connect an eBay account, you agree that eBay Inc. and its affiliates are third-party
      beneficiaries of these terms and may enforce them. You must use eBay data only as eBay’s user
      agreement and API terms allow, and you consent to us processing your eBay data to provide the
      service. eBay data is deleted within 30 days of an eBay account deletion notice, and within
      10 days if our eBay API access ends.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Amazon data rules</h2>
    <p>
      If you connect an Amazon account, Amazon’s data protection policy and acceptable use policy for
      selling partner data apply to you and your users. Buyer personal data from Amazon may be used
      only to fulfil orders and answer buyers, must not be exported or kept beyond what the service
      keeps, and is deleted within 30 days of delivery and within 30 days of disconnecting the
      account.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We provide the service with reasonable skill and care. Nothing in these terms limits liability
      for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else the law does
      not allow to be limited. Otherwise we are not liable for loss of profit, revenue or data, or
      for indirect loss, and our total liability in any 12 months is limited to the fees you paid us
      in that period. We are not responsible for Amazon, eBay, carriers or other third-party
      services.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Suspension and termination</h2>
    <p>
      We may suspend access to protect the service, other customers or a marketplace, or if these
      terms are broken, and will tell you why. You may stop using the service at any time. When an
      agreement ends we delete your workspace data as set out in our privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may change these terms. We update the date above, and users are asked to accept materially
      changed terms at their next sign-in.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and its courts have exclusive
      jurisdiction. Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.support}`}
        >{CONTACT.support}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
